  "body": "## What changed\nReserve a fresh directory for each bore fixture with atomic create_dir.\nSkip occupied numbered paths and report other creation errors.\nReserve the save/reopen output directory explicitly.\n\n## Cause\nThe failed CI artifact records PermissionDenied while writing plate.stl in all four reported tests.\nThe old helper reused a tag and process ID directory and ignored cleanup errors.\nA reused PID can select leftovers owned by another runner user.\n\n## Tests\nPin: bore_fixtures_preserve_existing_pid_paths_and_isolate_repeated_tags.\nThe pin failed on unchanged upstream/main 4d6b75e77 before the fix.\nRestoring upstream code with the pin retained made it fail again.\nRestoring the fix made it pass.\nAll six bore_core tests pass.\nThe final cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main passes.\nThe final cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings passes.\nThe first gate exposed the save/reopen test's implicit directory assumption.\nThe updated test now reserves that directory and passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\ngit diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\nSeparate operating system user accounts and the hosted CI rerun.\nThe pin models stale directories and repeated names in one process.\n\n## Overlaps\nNone found for crates/app/tests/bore_core.rs or the decision file.\n\nChangelog: Isolate bore test fixture directories from stale runner PID paths.\n\nEffort: low.\n\nFixes #3289\n",
